message: "Please cite this software when using the formal proofs or exact computational checks."
type: software
title: "BTP/PBF: formal proofs and exact computational checks"
authors:
  - family-names: "Mañas"
    given-names: "Manuel"
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0003-3764-5737"
date-released: "2026-10-25"
repository-code: "https://github.com/ManuelManas/btp-pbf-verification"
url: "https://github.com/ManuelManas/btp-pbf-verification/releases/tag/2026-10-25-audit-correspondence"
abstract: >-
  Lean proofs and manuscript-to-formalization correspondence for banded total
  positivity and positive bidiagonal factorizations. Includes inverse-minor
  existence criteria, Toeplitz factorization and the general analytic stability
  criteria in arbitrary bandwidth, with fixed or variable initial entries,
  and with arbitrary positive growth in entrywise relative norms. The actual
  products, inverse estimates, uniqueness and operator-norm comparison are
  proved. Exact hypotheses and remaining gaps in coverage are documented.
  Historical exact and high-precision computational checks are preserved.
  This release refreshes correspondence with the manuscript revised locally
  on 25 October 2026, rather than the currently posted arXiv version. The
  formal sources and recorded build and axiom audit remain those of
  19 October 2026; no Lean compilation or computational check was rerun.
